      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-85458",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following probabilities could be approximated using the Poisson approximation of the binomial distribution?\n\n1. The probability of getting $90$ heads on $200$ flips of a coin.\n2. The probability of getting a defective lightbulb in a package of $10$ if $2%$ of lightbulbs are defective.\n3. The probability of getting an egg with two yolks in a carton of $36$ eggs if $0.1%$ of eggs have two yolks."
